{"key": "3ebc05519e4aaf7d3c5698545e99537b48eae60f0a37bd748eca939b613956a3", "response": {"_call": {"failed_tries": [], "latency_s": 6.718, "request_id": "req_011CfvCekmfAS7wG8drdbagS", "ttft_s": 3.062}, "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"caller": {"type": "direct"}, "id": "toolu_016DJPzy2bZ297nvqcB9KNt8", "input": {"content": "\"\"\"Driver for the Brevalt KX-100 RF power meter. The programming manual is MANUAL.md.\n\n`session` is an open connection to the meter with three methods:\n    session.write(cmd: str) -> None\n    session.read() -> str\n    session.query(cmd: str) -> str      # write, then read\n\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InstrumentError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"The meter reported an error: SYST:ERR? returned a code other than 0.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _drain_errors(session) -> list[str]:\n    errors = []\n    for _ in range(20):  # the queue holds at most 10 entries\n        reply = session.query(\"SYST:ERR?\").strip()\n        if reply.split(\",\", 1)[0].strip().lstrip(\"+\") in (\"0\", \"-0\", \"00\"):\n            break\n        errors.append(reply)\n    return errors\n\n\ndef measure_power(session, freq_hz: float, averages: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Measure the power of a signal at `freq_hz`, averaging `averages` readings, and return it in dBm.\n\n    Raise InstrumentError if the meter reports any error while configuring or measuring.\n    \"\"\"\n    if float(averages).is_integer():\n        count = str(int(averages))\n    else:\n        count = repr(float(averages))  # let the meter refuse it (-104)\n\n    session.write(\"*CLS\")\n    session.write(f\"SENS:FREQ {float(freq_hz)!r}\")\n    session.write(f\"SENS:AVER:COUN {count}\")\n    session.write(\"CONF:POW:RANG AUTO\")\n    session.write(\"INIT\")\n    if session.query(\"*OPC?\").strip() != \"1\":\n        raise InstrumentError(\"measurement did not complete\")\n    reading = session.query(\"FETC?\").strip()\n\n    errors = _drain_errors(session)\n    if errors:\n        raise InstrumentError(\"; \".join(errors))\n\n    try:\n        value = float(reading)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise InstrumentError(f\"unparsable reading: {reading!r}\") from e\n    return value\n", "path": "driver.py"}, "name": "write_file", "toolset_name": null, "type": "tool_use"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CfvCem7zjEYkQkGmLayQ7", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 6644}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6644, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4752, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 990, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 252}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard"}}}
{"key": "d0539c0502b9487340ec7d3021249d00a334e207b67e3a3583ec8edd10159d26", "response": {"_call": {"failed_tries": [], "latency_s": 3.016, "request_id": "req_011CfvCfFdVcodAbmHk1zvzj", "ttft_s": 3.016}, "container": null, "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I implemented `measure_power` in `driver.py` following the manual's sequence in section 3. I didn't run it against the simulator; I only checked it by reading `kx100.py`.\n\n- **Sequence:** it sends `*CLS`, then sets the frequency and averaging count, then sets the range to AUTO. It then sends `INIT`, waits on `*OPC?`, and reads `FETC?`.\n- **Errors:** it empties the error queue with `SYST:ERR?`. If any error comes back, it raises `InstrumentError` listing them and returns no reading. That includes a refused setting such as a frequency outside 10 MHz to 18 GHz, and an over-range reading (error 201).\n- **Result:** otherwise it returns the `FETC?` reading as a `float` in dBm.\n\nA non-integer `averages` is sent as given, so the meter refuses it with error -104 and you get an `InstrumentError`.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CfvCfFya9jyttf5Z7Ud4n", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1009}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1009, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11396, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 306, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard"}}}
